<div class="nb info">The ISA is isothermal above 36,089 ft (11,000 m), so <b>a = 497.9 kt at every level from FL370 to FL450</b> - it stops falling with altitude. At 35,000 ft it is 500.5 kt (576.2 mph).</div>
<div class="tb"><table id="isa"><thead><tr><th>Altitude (ft)</th><th>a (kt)</th><th>a (mph)</th><th>T (deg C)</th><th>sigma</th><th>sqrt(sigma)</th><th>a*sqrt(sigma) (kt)</th><th>IAS at M0.76</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
